  "findings": [
    "Stage A's series ceiling replicates. Independent analogue series per receptor: MC1R 22, MC3R 22, MC4R 30, MC5R 14. Effective-sample-size ratios MC1R 0.061, MC3R 0.082, MC4R 0.048, MC5R 0.146. The ~30-series ceiling is a property of melanocortin peptide chemistry, not of the MC4R literature: no receptor's peptides resolve into many more independent series than MC4R's.",
    "The non-canonical residue burden replicates across receptors: MC1R 74.9%, MC3R 68.4%, MC4R 80.5%, MC5R 78.1%. Stage A measured 80.5% on MC4R; this is a class-wide property, so a representation restricted to the 20 canonical amino acids is inadequate for every receptor in the family, not just the one it was diagnosed on.",
    "Stage B's reversal finding does NOT replicate as stated. Contrasts reversing between the cross-series and within-series evaluations, per receptor: MC1R 3/5, MC3R 2/5, MC4R 5/5, MC5R 1/5. All five reverse only on MC4R. Stage B's claim that all five reverse was measured on one receptor and is therefore weaker than it reads: the direction of a representation contrast is partly a property of the particular receptor's data, so no single contrast result should be treated as a general fact about peptide representations.",
    "The best cross-series representation differs on every receptor: MC1R positional_fragment_fp__ridge, MC3R morgan_fp__forest, MC4R positional_fragment_fp+morgan_fp__ridge, MC5R residue_chemistry+positional_fragment_fp__ridge. 4 distinct winners across 4 receptors, so no representation wins twice. Stage B's representation ranking therefore does not transfer either: picking a representation on one receptor and applying it to another is not supported by these measurements.",
    "Cross-series MAE per receptor: MC1R 0.919, MC3R 0.827, MC4R 0.870, MC5R 0.974. Deployment gate: failed by every receptor. The gate is unchanged and is evaluated per single-target dataset; expanding to the family did not move MC4R's result, because MC4R's own records are identical to what Stage B already used.",
    "The gate is a conjunction, and that matters here: MC1R R2 +0.397 clears the R2 >= 0.30 criterion, but its MAE 0.919 does not clear MAE <= 0.70, so it does not pass. A receptor can rank molecules better than MC4R's model while still being too inaccurate per molecule to publish a number.",
    "Abstentions: MC2R (abstained, 0 peptides). Below 40 traced peptides neither the clustering nor the cross-series split has enough independent groups to support a number, so none is reported.",
    "Study grouping is coarse in this corpus. The 39 documents behind the peptide rows collapse into 17 leak-free study groups, the largest holding 43.9% of rows (203 molecules). Molecules are re-measured across papers, so a leak-free study group is a connected component of the (molecule, document) graph rather than a single document. A study-grouped holdout therefore cannot be tuned to a target size: whole components move, and the giant component is either wholly in or wholly out."
  ],
